# Original generation prompt

Use case: scientific-educational.
Asset type: original raster PNG learning-goal illustration for German Gymnasium introductory chemistry, native landscape near 1600 x 900 or close 16:9. Friendly abstract comic classroom illustration, warm cream, navy outlines, soft cheerful colours matching SkillPilot chemistry visualizations. All important elements and very short headings remain clear at 360 px image width; avoid dense text, small-print facts or a cluttered infographic.
Whole goal: Describe significance and uses of acids and acidic aqueous solutions in everyday life using supplied examples and match handling rules to supplied substance/hazard information. It is introductory material-based matching, not a recipe, pH calculation, advanced mechanism, experiment, or blanket product safety authorization.
Create a simple illustrated flow with three large connected concept areas. Left: two separate ingredient cards labelled "Citronensäure" and "Wasser" point into one closed clear bottle labelled "Saure Lösung"; this shows the acid is a COMPONENT of the aqueous solution, not that water and an acid symbol are the same thing. Keep physical objects generic and schematic; do not claim a particular concentration or hazard classification. Centre: an example card labelled "Verwendung" with a pictorial view of limescale being removed from a clearly glazed ceramic surface, next to a magnifying glass checking the applicable material/instruction card. Caption in large print: "Eignung prüfen". Do NOT show somebody pouring a cleaner or an instruction to apply it to any surface; this is a supplied example illustration of a use that depends on material and product information. Right: a large card labelled "Umgang" showing the closed classroom chemical bottle beside protective goggles and a readable information-card icon; a crossed-out mouth/tasting icon and a crossed-out mixing-two-bottles icon demonstrate two distinct supplied classroom rules. Caption "Angaben beachten". All containers remain closed; no tasting, skin testing or mixing is performed, no food/drink posing as laboratory chemical.
Exact short title: "Saure Lösungen im Alltag". The illustration should visually connect substance information, suitable use and appropriate handling of the same selected sample, without saying all acids or all citric-acid solutions are harmless, corrosive, identical or used identically. A small single environmental water/plant vignette can show another everyday significance only if layout remains very simple; otherwise omit it. No pH-scale wall, no molecular mechanism, no formula calculations, no lengthy warning block, no human release badge, no photos, watermark or brand.

